    "input": "\"{\\\"message\\\": \\\"Use websearch agent.\\\"}\"",
    "output": "\"**Professor Oak:** Excellent idea, trainer! I've used the Web Search Agent to find the most up-to-date and comprehensive list of the **Top 10 Strongest Water Pokémon of All Time (2024)**. This includes legendary powerhouses and competitive favorites that are dominating the metagame right now!\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🌊 **Top 10 Strongest Water Pokémon of All Time (2024)**\\n\\n| Rank | Pokémon | Type | Base Stat Total (Form) | Key Strengths |\\n|------|---------|------|------------------------|---------------|\\n| **1** | **Primal Kyogre** | Water | **770** | Highest raw damage, permanent rain, +50% Water move power, massive Sp. Attack |\\n| **2** | **Palkia** | Water/Dragon | **680** | Highest non-legendary stats, 150 Sp. Attack, 100 Speed, Dragon typing |\\n| **3** | **Kyogre** | Water | **670** | Drizzle ability, 150 Power Water Spout, extreme power, signature legendary |\\n| **4** | **Volcanion** | Fire/Water | **600** | 130 Sp. Attack, Steam Eruption (110 Power), Water Absorb healing |\\n| **5** | **Swampert (Mega)** | Water/Ground | **700** | 150 Attack, only 1 weakness (Grass), immune to Electric, unkillable bulk |\\n| **6** | **Greninja** | Water/Dark | **530** | 120 Speed, Battle Bond form, protean versatility, Ash-Greninja in anime |\\n| **7** | **Toxapex** | Water/Poison | **485** | 152 Defense, stall king, Recover + Baneful Bunker, competitive nightmare |\\n| **8** | **Gyarados** | Water/Flying | **540** | 125 Attack, Dragon Dance sweeper, Intimidate, Mega Evolution available |\\n| **9** | **Blastoise (Mega)** | Water | **630** | Classic tank, Mega Evolution boosts, high Defense/Sp. Defense |\\n| **10** | **Kingdra** | Water/Dragon | **540** | Balanced 95 stats, Rain Dance sweeper, Dragon typing for coverage |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🏆 **Key Highlights from the Web Search**\\n\\n#### **1. Primal Kyogre - The Undisputed King**\\n- **Stat Total: 770** (highest of any Water-type)\\n- **Ability:** Primordial Sea (creates permanent rain, boosts Water moves 50%)\\n- **Signature Move:** Water Spout (150 Power, scales with HP)\\n- **Trivia:** Primal Kyogre is considered the **strongest Water-type ever created** and dominates both competitive play and lore.\\n\\n#### **2. Palkia - The Spatial Dragon**\\n- **Stat Total: 680** (highest non-Primal/non-Mega Water-type)\\n- **Typing:** Water/Dragon (only weak to Dragon and Fairy)\\n- **Role:** Special sweeper with 150 Sp. Attack and 100 Speed\\n- **Trivia:** Represents space itself and can distort dimensions!\\n\\n#### **3. Kyogre - The Weather Control Master**\\n- **Stat Total: 670** (Standard form)\\n- **Ability:** Drizzle (sets rain on entry)\\n- **Signature Move:** Water Spout (150 Power)\\n- **Trivia:** One of the original Weather Trio legendaries from Hoenn.\\n\\n#### **4. Volcanion - The Steam Pokémon**\\n- **Unique Typing:** Fire/Water (only Pokémon with this combo!)\\n- **Signature Move:** Steam Eruption (110 Power, 30% burn chance)\\n- **Ability:** Water Absorb (heals HP when hit by Water moves)\\n- **Trivia:** Mythical Pokémon with incredible mixed attacking potential.\\n\\n#### **5. Mega Swampert - The Unkillable Tank**\\n- **Stat Total: 700** (Mega form)\\n- **Typing:** Water/Ground (only weak to Grass, 4x resistant to Rock)\\n- **Ability:** Swift Swim (doubles Speed in rain)\\n- **Trivia:** In rain teams, Mega Swampert becomes nearly unstoppable with 150 Attack and doubled Speed!\\n\\n#### **6. Greninja - The Speed Demon**\\n- **Speed: 120** (among the fastest Water-types)\\n- **Battle Bond:** Transform after KOing an opponent (Ash-Greninja form)\\n- **Protean:** Changes type to match its move (versatile coverage)\\n- **Trivia:** Ash's Greninja in the anime was so powerful it could rival legendaries!\\n\\n#### **7. Toxapex - The Stall King**\\n- **Defense: 152** (one of the highest in the game)\\n- **Moves:** Recover, Baneful Bunker, Toxic Spikes, Scald\\n- **Role:** Competitive stall monster that frustrates opponents\\n- **Trivia:** The ultimate defensive Pokémon in Water/Poison typing.\\n\\n#### **8. Gyarados - The Classic Dragon**\\n- **Attack: 125** (massive physical power)\\n- **Dragon Dance:** Boosts Attack and Speed in one turn\\n- **Intimidate:** Lowers opponent's Attack on entry\\n- **Trivia:** One of the original pseudo-legendary Water-types from Gen 1.\\n\\n#### **9. Mega Blastoise - The Cannon Tank**\\n- **Stat Total: 630** (Mega form)\\n- **Mega Launcher:** Boosts pulse and projectile moves by 50%\\n- **Signature:** Massive cannons on its back for artillery bombardment\\n- **Trivia:** The original starter Water-type, now with Mega Evolution power!\\n\\n#### **10. Kingdra - The Rain Sweeper**\\n- **Balanced Stats:** 95 in Attack, Sp. Attack, Defense, and Sp. Defense\\n- **Dragon/Water typing:** Only weak to Dragon and Fairy\\n- **Rain Dance:** Boosts Water moves significantly\\n- **Trivia:** Evolves from Seadra with Dragon Scale, a fan-favorite for rain teams!\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🌟 **Professor Oak's Analysis**\\n\\nThis list shows the **evolution of Water-type dominance** across generations! From the legendary titans like **Primal Kyogre** and **Palkia** to competitive staples like **Toxapex** and **Greninja**, Water-types have consistently been among the strongest Pokémon.\\n\\n**Key Trends:**\\n- **Legendaries Dominate:** Primal Kyogre, Palkia, and standard Kyogre are in a league of their own\\n- **Mega Evolutions Matter:** Mega Swampert and Mega Blastoise show how evolution can transform Water-types\\n- **Competitive Staples:** Toxapex and Greninja dominate the modern metagame\\n- **Unique Typings:** Volcanion (Fire/Water) and Gyarados (Water/Flying) offer special advantages\\n\\n**Which Water-type is YOUR favorite?** Would you like me to dive deeper into any of these aquatic champions, or perhaps explore their battle strategies? 🌊\"",
    "createdAt": "2026-04-04T20:05:09.000Z",
